  "description": "HOPMUX crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P n n 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C139 H173 Eu3 O34 Ti3,C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Ti1 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti2 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors; Ti3 (Ti) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.242-4.268 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.21-136.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu3Ti3(μ3-O)2(μ3-OH)(CH3O)2(Ac)2(CH3OH)(tbba)12]·CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
